From 9ca96f3318d0c6ea512cfbd531e79181946cad1d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dominick Morales <dmorales2024@my.fit.edu>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 13:00:19 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] KVM: introspection: core and message handling

Hook/unhook, the receiving thread, per-vCPU jobs and the request loop,
VM and vCPU commands, and the gfn access table.

Changes from kvmi-v7: vCPU waits use the vCPU rcuwait; the receiving
thread borrows the VMM mm for guest memory access; access restrictions
live in a gfn-indexed xarray instead of per-memslot bitmaps, so they
survive memslot changes; message buffers are whitelisted for usercopy.

Based on the Bitdefender KVMI patches (kvmi-v7, kvmi-v12).
